# Created by https://www.gitignore.io/api/phpstorm,composer
# Edit at https://www.gitignore.io/?templates=phpstorm,composer

### Composer ###
composer.phar
/vendor/

# The lock file is committed on purpose. Without it CI resolves dependencies from scratch on every
# run, and Composer refuses to resolve firebase/php-jwt because of the advisories against every
# version of it, which leaves no installable set of packages at all.
#
# The lock pins firebase/php-jwt v6.11.1, which is listed under the disputed CVE-2025-45769. That
# advisory is about HMAC secret strength and short RSA keys. This framework only signs APNs
# authorization tokens with ES256, so it is not affected. Revisit when a fixed 6.x is published.

